{"slug":"the-fast-and-the-furious","title":"The Fast and the Furious","desc":"PS2, Eutechnyx 2006 (USA)","notes":["Folder names are the game's file codes.  A car of this game is built from parts: this is the STOCK set (body, bonnet, front / rear bumper, head / tail lights, mirrors, windows, boot, spoiler when the car has one) + 4 wheels.","The game keeps NO tyre in its files, only the rim: the black tyres are plain placeholders (radius from the game's vehicle script).  The body colour is grey: the game paints it at run time.","The game has about 125 entries for cars, but most of them are variants (other paint / body kit) that use the parts of another car and have none of their own: only the cars with a complete set of parts are here.","BODY KITS: every kit part of the game (all styles of body, bonnet, front / rear bumper, side skirts, spoiler, mirrors, boot, head / tail lights) is in the hidden 'Variants' folder of <code>.fbx, a subfolder per kind of part, named <kind>_<style>_... (the style numbers are the game's: 02NSXRTR20_FRBUMPER is 'frbumper_20').  Hidden objects are easy to miss, so every car also has <code>_kits.fbx: the stock car and then one complete car per kit style, all VISIBLE, in rows of 6 (folders 'stock', 'kit_20', 'kit_22' ...).  Take the one you want or copy its folder out.","RIMS: the folder _Rims holds every rim of the game as a file of its own (the shop rims, the stock rim of each car, the rims of the kits), one rim per folder, standing on the ground, outer face towards +X (placeholder: no tyre).  Brakes and exhausts are not included."],"tags":["the-fast-and-the-furious"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["01EVO7GSR","",18376817,"the-fast-and-the-furious","car-01EVO7GSR.zip","thumbs/the-fast-and-the-furious/cars/car-01EVO7GSR.webp"],["02FLADYZST","",21575218,"the-fast-and-the-furious","car-02FLADYZST.zip","thumbs/the-fast-and-the-furious/cars/car-02FLADYZST.webp"],["02NSXRTR","",6277508,"the-fast-and-the-furious","car-02NSXRTR.